.Dd $Mdocdate: September 21 2026 $
.Dt RTRD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rtrd
.Nd RPKI-to-Router (RTR) daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm rtrd
.Op Fl fvV
.Op Fl b Ar bind_address
.Op Fl m Ar max_version
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon is an RPKI-to-Router (RTR) cache server.
The
.Nm
program supports RTR protocol versions 0, 1, and 2.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b Ar bind_address
Use
.Ar bind_address
as the listener address for connections from clients.
The default
.Ar bind_address
is
.Sq 0.0.0.0 .
.It Fl f
Remain in foreground.
.It Fl m Ar max_version
Use
.Ar max_version
as the maximum supported version in protocol version negotiation.
The default protocol is version 2.
.It Fl p Ar port
Listen on
.Ar port
for client connections.
The default port is 323.
.It Fl s Ar socket
Use
.Ar socket
instead of the default
.Pa /var/run/rtrd.sock
for communication with
.Xr rtrctl 8 .
.It Fl v
Increase verbosity.
.It Fl V
Display version and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/rtrd.sock" -compact
.It Pa /var/run/rtrd.sock
Unix-domain socket used for communication with
.Xr rtrctl 8 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bgpd.conf 5 ,
.Xr bgpd 8 ,
.Xr rpki-client 8 ,
.Xr rtrctl 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T RPKI to Router Protocol
.%R RFC 6810
.Re
.Pp
.Rs
.%T RPKI to Router Protocol, Version 1
.%R RFC 8210
.Re
.Pp
.Rs
.%T RPKI to Router Protocol, Version 2
.%U https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-sidrops-8210bis-27
.%D Aug, 2026
.Re
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
daemon first appeared in
.Ox 8.0 .
